::

Mark all read is the icon-only title-row double-check (G3 pass, WP-N3 08-11) — old label as `aria-label`, verb unchanged. Every notification row deep-links to its source surface (a message notification opens Messages, a build notification opens the app, a task notification opens the task). Unread rows carry the RIGHT-SIDE blue accent dot — accent left border is BANNED as an unread treatment. The hub sheet's Notifications row shows the unread count. Preference toggles render as rows carrying the ON/OFF state in the title with a `toggled` hook and a stable toggle verb — the form grammar has no checkbox item today.

::callout[type=note title="Renderer note — deferred"]
The shipped preference control is a toggle SWITCH per row (coverage matrix, Toggle switches row). Rows with the ON/OFF state in the title stand in; the live switch is the state layer + planned toggle treatment.
::

## Quiet hours sheet

Defined ONCE in `modals/quiet-hours.surf` (`name=quiet-hours`), via the Quiet hours row (`openQuietHours`): start/end times, day toggles, urgent-mention breakthrough. This file carries no inline copy.
